# DTF tier manifest: oci-manifests-reconcile
#   artifact-keeper#1683 (1.12.0): the oci_manifests existence table is
#   reconciled at startup and every OCI_MANIFESTS_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECS.
#
# Profile-set: filesystem + gc.oci-manifests-reconcile-fast (new:
# OCI_MANIFESTS_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_SECS=15; the default is six hours).
# Images are pushed over /v2 with curl (config, one layer, a curl-built OCI
# manifest), as trash-blob-gc-remote-cache does.
#
# THE CHANGE
# Migration 268 (1.11.x) added `oci_manifests`, one row per (repository,
# manifest digest), written in the push transaction and removed by the
# delete unwind when the last tag goes (#4512, 1.11.0). Rows still drift:
# the lifecycle tag prune (lifecycle_service CASCADE_OCI_TAGS_SQL) deletes
# oci_tags and soft-deletes the manifest artifact without touching
# oci_manifests, a pre-268 replica's delete or push during a rolling
# upgrade leaves a row behind or none at all, and the backfill that adds
# missing rows runs once, at startup. Since #1683 a reconcile pass runs at
# startup and on the interval: it removes a row whose manifest is no longer
# addressable (no oci_tags row, no index edge from a tagged or live parent,
# no live artifacts row at oci-manifests/<digest> or with its checksum)
# once the row's last_referenced_at is older than 600 s, and it adds the
# row of a tagged manifest that has none.
#
# THE PRIMITIVES
#   One docker repository, five tagged images. The lifecycle case backdates
#   the image's oci_tags.updated_at and its manifest artifact's created_at
#   ten days with SQL (the max_age_days clock) and runs a max_age_days
#   policy (days=5) explicitly assigned to the repository. The reconcile's
#   600 s minimum row age is met by moving last_referenced_at an hour back
#   with SQL, which stands in for time passing. The backend is never
#   restarted, so 1.11.5's startup backfill cannot be what re-adds a row.
#
# THE GATES (RED ak-backend:1.11.5, GREEN on the #1683 image)
#   (CONTROL)  both images: deleting an image's only tag over /v2 removes
#              its row (#4512) and GET by digest is 404; the lifecycle policy
#              prunes the expired image's tag, soft-deletes its manifest
#              artifact, and GET by digest is 404, leaving the other images
#              live; after the reconcile passes a tagged image and an
#              untagged image whose artifacts row is live (its oci_tags row
#              deleted with SQL) both keep their rows.
#   (FIX)      the expired image's row is removed within 75 s (five
#              intervals); RED on 1.11.5: the row stays, unaddressable.
#              The row of a tagged image, deleted with SQL, is back within
#              75 s with size_bytes = the manifest body length; RED on
#              1.11.5: no row until the next restart.
#   ak_oci_manifests_reconcile_rows_removed_total is reported, not gated.
#
# Wall clock: about 2.5 min (75 s wait on 1.11.5, then 35 s so the keep
# controls are read after two more passes).
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: not under test.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem gc.oci-manifests-reconcile-fast"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
